 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in Senate",
   "date": "1996-06-11",
   "text": "Auto Choice Reform Act of 1996 - Authorizes consumers of motor vehicle insurance to choose between present tort liability coverage for personal injury under the State's financial responsibility law or, in lieu thereof, insurance that combines first-party insurance and the right to sue negligent drivers for all further uncompensated economic losses. Sets forth certain requirements for such policies."
  }
